% ============================================================
% ABSTRACT (Professional IEEE Conference Abstract)
% ============================================================
\begin{abstract}
The convergence of Tiny Machine Learning (TinyML) and cloud-hosted Large Language Models (LLMs) provides a transformative paradigm for intelligent edge computing, enabling microcontroller-class devices to deliver human-like conversational experiences without the prohibitive computational overhead of local foundation model execution. This paper presents the architecture, engineering deployment, and empirical evaluation of an advanced edge-assisted multimodal conversational agent built upon the UNIHIKER K10 single-board platform (powered by an Espressif ESP32-S3 dual-core SoC) and running the open-source \textit{xiaozhi-esp32} firmware framework integrated with the DeepSeek language reasoning model. Unlike conventional single-language microcontroller interfaces, the proposed system natively supports bilingual voice interaction in both English and Hindi with seamless code-switching, Devanagari acoustic handling, and contextual response generation.

The system leverages on-device voice activity detection (VAD) and Opus-compressed full-duplex WebSocket streaming to relay user utterances to a cloud gateway, which coordinates multilingual speech-to-text (STT), DeepSeek-V3/R1 semantic reasoning, and low-latency neural text-to-speech (TTS) streaming back to the onboard I2S audio amplifier and speaker. Furthermore, the platform integrates an onboard camera for multimodal visual recognition (e.g., answering queries such as ``What are you looking at?'') with real-time frame rendering on its 2.8-inch color LCD, alongside voice-actuated hardware peripheral control mediated by the Model Context Protocol (MCP) to dynamically command onboard RGB LED arrays. Empirical evaluations reveal an average end-to-end round-trip latency of 1482\,ms for English and 1618\,ms for Hindi, while maintaining peak internal SRAM consumption below 308\,KB (60.2\%) and total power draw under 1.45\,W during active streaming. This work provides an open, reproducible reference design for low-cost, multilingual, and multimodal edge AI conversational terminals.
\end{abstract}

\begin{IEEEkeywords}
TinyML, Edge AI, UNIHIKER K10, ESP32-S3, DeepSeek LLM, Xiaozhi AI, Multilingual Speech Processing, Hindi Voice Assistant, Multimodal Vision, Model Context Protocol (MCP), WebSocket Streaming.
\end{IEEEkeywords}

