\section{System Architecture and Implementation}

\subsection{Hardware Architecture of the UNIHIKER K10}
The UNIHIKER K10 (DFRobot DFR0992-EN) integrates a rich set of input/output peripherals centered around the Espressif ESP32-S3 SoC:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Processing Core:} Dual-core 32-bit Xtensa LX7 processor operating at 240~MHz with integrated vector instructions, 512~KB internal SRAM, and 16~MB external pseudo-static RAM (PSRAM) accessed via high-speed Octal SPI (OPI).
    \item \textbf{Visual Display:} 2.8-inch TFT LCD color display with a native resolution of 240$\times$320 pixels, driven by an ST7789 controller over high-speed SPI with DMA support, utilized to display animated facial expressions, chat history, network status, and captured camera images.
    \item \textbf{Imaging Sensor:} Onboard front-facing CMOS camera (GC0308 sensor, up to 640$\times$480 VGA resolution) connected via parallel DVP interface, dedicated to capturing visual context for multimodal inference.
    \item \textbf{Audio Subsystem:} Digital omnidirectional I2S MEMS microphone for acoustic voice capture, alongside an onboard Maxim MAX98357A Class-D audio amplifier driving an integrated 1~W miniature speaker.
    \item \textbf{Tactile User Interface:} Two tactile pushbuttons: Button~A (short press: wake-up/speech interrupt; long press $\ge 1$\,s: volume increment) and Button~B (short press: wake-up/speech interrupt; long press $\ge 1$\,s: volume decrement).
    \item \textbf{Visual Actuation:} Built-in addressable WS2812 RGB LED ring controllable via GPIO using the ESP32 RMT (Remote Control) peripheral, supporting dynamic status indications and voice-driven Model Context Protocol (MCP) actuation.
    \item \textbf{Wireless Connectivity:} 2.4~GHz Wi-Fi (802.11~b/g/n) and Bluetooth 5.0 (BLE) supporting long-range communications and SoftAP onboarding.
\end{itemize}

