\subsection{Firmware Deployment and AP Network Onboarding Methodology}
Deployment of the conversational firmware onto the UNIHIKER K10 follows a robust three-stage workflow:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Binary Flashing via UART:} The UNIHIKER K10 is placed in bootloader mode by holding the onboard \textit{BOOT} button while applying power via USB Type-C. Using the Espressif Flash Download Tool, the configuration is set to Chip Type: \texttt{ESP32-S3}, WorkMode: \texttt{Develop}, and LoadMode: \texttt{UART}. The pre-compiled English/multilingual firmware binary (\texttt{xiaozhi-1.8.5-unihikerk10-ENver.bin}) is mapped to flash address \texttt{0x00000000}. A full flash erase is performed before writing at 1,152,000~baud to prevent partition table corruptions.
    \item \textbf{Captive Portal SoftAP Onboarding:} Upon resetting the board via the \textit{RST} button, the firmware detects the absence of stored Wi-Fi credentials in Non-Volatile Storage (NVS) and launches an open SoftAP network (SSID: \texttt{xiaozhi-xxxxxx}). The user connects via smartphone or computer, accesses the captive portal interface at \texttt{192.168.4.1}, and inputs the 2.4~GHz Wi-Fi SSID and security key. Credentials are securely committed to NVS, and the device restarts automatically.
    \item \textbf{Cloud Gateway Binding:} Upon establishing an Internet connection, the UNIHIKER K10 contacts the Xiaozhi cloud backend (\url{https://xiaozhi.me/}) and renders a dynamic, unique 6-digit alphanumeric pairing code on its 2.8-inch LCD screen. The developer logs into the Xiaozhi Management Console, enters the displayed code, and associates the device with their account. In this console, the underlying foundation model is configured to \textbf{DeepSeek} (DeepSeek-V3 / DeepSeek-R1), the voice synthesizer is chosen, and the system prompt is injected.
\end{enumerate}

