\subsection{Multilingual Conversational Pipeline: English and Hindi Voice Handling}
A major architectural breakthrough of this deployment is its native bilingual operational capability. Language handling is managed across a synchronized edge-cloud pipeline:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Edge Acoustic Capture:} Audio is sampled via I2S at 16~kHz, 16-bit mono PCM. A lightweight energy-entropy VAD algorithm detects speech onset and termination. Spoken audio chunks are compressed in real time using the Opus codec (bitrate: 16--24~kbps) and streamed over WebSocket binary frames to minimize network egress payload.
    \item \textbf{Cloud Multilingual STT:} The Xiaozhi cloud gateway directs incoming Opus audio to a multilingual ASR engine (FunASR/Whisper-large-v3). The acoustic model processes both English phonemes and Hindi phonetic structures (including Devanagari script representations and Romanized phonetic transcripts) without requiring the user to manually toggle languages.
    \item \textbf{DeepSeek Cross-Lingual Reasoning:} The transcribed text is injected into the DeepSeek conversational context. The system prompt is engineered to enforce natural bilingual code-switching:
    \begin{quote}
    \small \texttt{"You are a helpful AI assistant running on UNIHIKER K10. You are fully fluent in both English and Hindi. If the user speaks in English, respond in clear English. If the user speaks in Hindi, respond in fluent Hindi using Devanagari script. If the user uses mixed Hinglish, respond conversationally in natural Hinglish."}
    \end{quote}
    DeepSeek's extensive pretraining on cross-lingual data enables it to grasp cultural idioms, technical jargon, and grammatical structures in both languages effortlessly.
    \item \textbf{Neural TTS Synthesis:} The generated response tokens are streamed to a high-speed neural TTS synthesizer supporting dual-language acoustic profiles (e.g., CosyVoice or Azure Speech Indian English and Hindi neural voices). The synthesized audio is returned to the UNIHIKER K10 as Opus-compressed audio frames, decoded on Core~1, and played through the MAX98357A I2S amplifier.
\end{enumerate}

