\subsection{Acoustic Robustness and Multilingual Recognition Accuracy}
Table~\ref{tab:acoustic_accuracy} documents speech recognition error rates across noise conditions for both languages, reporting Word Error Rate (WER) for English and both WER and Character Error Rate (CER) for Hindi.

\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\caption{Acoustic Robustness Under Ambient Noise Profiles}
\label{tab:acoustic_accuracy}
\resizebox{0.95\columnwidth}{!}{%
\begin{tabular}{lcccc}
\toprule
\textbf{Acoustic Environment} & \textbf{SPL} & \textbf{English WER} & \textbf{Hindi WER} & \textbf{Hindi CER} \\
\midrule
Quiet Laboratory Setting      & 35~dB & 4.2\% & 5.8\% & 2.1\% \\
Active Classroom / Office     & 55~dB & 8.6\% & 10.4\% & 4.3\% \\
High Ambient Noise (Cafeteria)& 70~dB & 18.2\% & 22.8\% & 9.8\% \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}%
}
\end{table}

Under quiet and typical office conditions ($\le 55$\,dB SPL), the system delivers outstanding transcription accuracy, with English WER remaining below 8.6\% and Hindi WER below 10.4\% (with Hindi Character Error Rate remaining at an exceptional 4.3\%). In high-noise scenarios (70~dB SPL), acoustic degradation causes recognition error rates to rise, with Hindi experiencing a slightly higher impact due to masking of soft nasalized and aspirated consonants.

\subsection{Multimodal Visual Q\&A and MCP Actuation Benchmarks}
To answer \textbf{RQ$_3$}, Table~\ref{tab:mcp_benchmarks} summarizes performance metrics for visual Q\&A and Model Context Protocol hardware commands.

\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\caption{Performance Benchmarks for Vision and MCP Control}
\label{tab:mcp_benchmarks}
\resizebox{0.95\columnwidth}{!}{%
\begin{tabular}{lccc}
\toprule
\textbf{Command Category / Modality} & \textbf{Success Rate} & \textbf{Edge Latency} & \textbf{Total Turnaround} \\
\midrule
Visual Q\&A (``What are you looking at?'') & 94.0\% & 142~ms & 1580 $\pm$ 72~ms \\
MCP LED Control (All lights to blue)       & 98.5\% & 18~ms  & 495 $\pm$ 24~ms \\
MCP LED Control (Specific pixel index)     & 96.0\% & 18~ms  & 524 $\pm$ 28~ms \\
